<h2 class="sect">What it is</h2>
<dl class="mats">
  <div class="row"><dt>The work</dt>
    <dd>One project, carried out individually
      <span class="ms">You choose a question, find data, apply methods from the course, and write it up. The project is the whole assessment for this course.</span></dd></div>
  <div class="row"><dt>What you hand in</dt>
    <dd>A paper, the data, the code, and a 15-minute recording
      <span class="ms">The paper is about ten pages in the SIAM conference style, with eight required sections. The recording presents the project in your own voice.</span></dd></div>
  <div class="row"><dt>Two dates</dt>
    <dd>A 200-word proposal, then the project
      <span class="ms">The proposal is signed off by the teaching team before you start work. Dates are confirmed at the start of the semester and announced here and on Moodle at the same time.</span></dd></div>
  <div class="row"><dt>AI tools</dt>
    <dd>Allowed, and expected — but declared
      <span class="ms">Use assistants for code and prose. List every tool you used, and what you used it for, in the appendix. Undeclared use is misconduct; declared use is normal practice.</span></dd></div>
  <div class="row"><dt>If the result is negative</dt>
    <dd>An honest null result can score full marks
      <span class="ms">A hypothesis that data does not support is a real finding, and a well-told account of why it failed is worth more than a result that was helped along.</span></dd></div>
</dl>

<h2 class="sect" style="margin-top:2rem">The two documents</h2>
<dl class="mats">
  <div class="row"><dt>Requirements</dt>
    <dd><a href="materials/project/project-requirements.pdf">Requirements for the semester project (PDF)</a>
      <span class="ms">The binding text: deadlines, what is submitted, how it is assessed. Where this page and the requirements differ, the requirements are what counts.</span></dd></div>
  <div class="row"><dt>Shipping guidelines</dt>
    <dd><a href="materials/project/project-shipping-guidelines.pdf">Shipping your project (PDF)</a>
      <span class="ms">Practical advice, and not binding: folder layout, the README, reproducibility, the recording, and the one test to run before you submit.</span></dd></div>
</dl>

<h2 class="sect" style="margin-top:2rem">Gallery</h2>
<p style="color:var(--ink-2);max-width:62ch">Selected projects are published here, with their authors' permission
and credited to them. Consent is asked for at submission, is entirely optional, and has no bearing
on the grade.</p>
<p style="color:var(--ink-2);max-width:62ch">The gallery opens with the first consenting projects from this cohort.
Until then, the requirements above describe the standard the work is held to.</p>
